steps:
src/component/tooltip/TooltipHTMLContent.ts — `TooltipHTMLContent.dispose()` (baseline lines 549-562). Replace the element-removal block, currently lines 556-559:

```
        if (this.el) {
            const parentNode = this.el.parentNode;
            parentNode && parentNode.removeChild(this.el);
        }
```

with a version that hoists `this.el` into a local and explicitly unbinds the handlers first:

```
        const el = this.el;
        if (el) {
            el.onmouseenter = el.onmousemove = el.onmouseleave = null;
            const parentNode = el.parentNode;
            parentNode && parentNode.removeChild(el);
        }
```

Leave lines 550-554 (`clearTimeout(this._hideTimeout)`, `clearTimeout(this._longHideTimeout)`, `const zr = this._zr;`, `transformLocalCoordClear(...)`) and the trailing `this.el = this._container = null;` (line 561) exactly as they are. This is byte-for-byte the upstream fix (apache/echarts PR #21087, squashed as commits 6e5a8a7…/59ac414 under merge dbee785). The `if (el)` guard is required because the constructor short-circuits with `return null;` when `env.wxa` is true (line 305-307), leaving `this.el` undefined.
